/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flash13_acetic_ethanol_vacuum_flash -- the reactive flash that FLASHES,
  now on the MIXED-SOLVENT v1 surface.

  flash12's chemistry, volatile-rich (12 % ethanol), pulled to 0.65 atm at
  358.15 K.  The liquid declares `activityModel { ionic davies; molecular
  NRTL; }`: the molecular backbone (water + ethanol) is priced by the FULL
  curated NRTL pair -- gamma_EtOH = 2.97 at the feed, tripling the ideal
  volatility -- while the ions stay Davies on water-referenced molality
  and the solvent activity decomposes multiplicatively
  (a_w = gamma_w x_w * aw_ionic; the network K's stay water-referenced,
  the transfer term is the NAMED next slice).  The two-phase Newton
  couples all of it with the acetic vapour DIMER re-weighting the vapour
  balance (v_HAc = t_mono + 2 t_dim) and its association heat priced
  exactly into the duty.

  What the student sees: V/F = 0.580; y_EtOH = 0.193; the BUFFER HOLDS THE
  AMMONIA (99.94 % liquid-bound as NH4+, y_NH3 = 6e-4) while the liquid pH
  rises 4.62 -> 5.03; dimer share 12 %, -1.03 kW association heat inside
  the 669 kW duty.  Sum of vapour partials = P identically.  Compare with
  flash12 (same chemistry, ideal-authorised route, subsaturated): the
  gamma is the difference between a flash and no flash at all.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoSolve;
description  "Reactive VACUUM flash on mixed-solvent v1 (NRTL backbone + Davies ions): V/F = 0.58 at 358.15 K / 0.65 atm, gamma_EtOH = 2.97, the buffer holds the ammonia, dimer heat priced exactly";
verbosity     3;

reports
{
    streamTable    { }
    massBalance    { }
}
